1
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:10,750
Inu!

2
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:11,663
Hey, lady.

3
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:13,480
Hope I'm not too late.

4
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:18,980
Please! Silica!

5
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:23,040
You're here!

6
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:24,700
I can't believe it!

7
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:26,577
We couldn't send this one out.

8
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,307
We came as soon as we could.

9
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:31,137
Have you seen yourself lately?

10
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:33,177
You're all torn up.

11
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:35,357
You push yourself way too hard!

12
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:37,377
We brought everyone with us.

13
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,180
We can take it from here!

14
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:41,130
Everyone?

15
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:59,297
Those big stun ones are the bad guys!

16
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:00,800
Vanguard, with me!

17
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:02,420
Drive them back!

18
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:04,370
Rearguard?

19
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,641
Fall back with the Underworld!

20
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:07,857
Check your spells!

21
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:10,980
Just so we're clear, this
ain't nothing personal.

22
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:14,617
All the same, you're gonna pay
for what you did to our friend.

23
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:16,000
You'll pay big time.

24
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:20,500
Alright, now that that's settled,
here comes the pain, you bastards!

25
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,560
I'm not going to be able to run away.

26
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:48,740
I'm not going to be able to run away.

27
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:53,537
Look, I'm not going to
be able to run away.

28
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:55,117
I don't know if I'm not sure.

29
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:58,417
I don't know about what you can do.

30
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:01,617
But I don't have to worry about something.

31
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:04,837
I don't have to worry about it.

32
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:08,740
It's simply very important to difference.

33
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:10,880
You knew you might not get them back,
but still, you converted your characters.

34
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:13,380
I just, I'm sorry.

35
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:15,337
What are you talking about, Asuna?

36
00:03:15,420 --> 00:03:18,440
Why do you think we work
so hard in SAO and ALO4?

37
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:22,466
It's this, to protect the people
we love whenever and wherever.

38
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,660
You're right, as usual.

39
00:03:28,420 --> 00:03:29,250
Thanks, guys.

40
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:32,789
Wait, the Underworld's
on a closed network.

41
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:34,881
Who told you how to log on to it?

42
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:38,220
I'm surprised you'd ask.

43
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:39,657
It should be obvious.

44
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:40,740
Yeah, it was Yui.

45
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:44,657
She told us everything that was going
on with the Underworld and its people.

46
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:47,387
We've never seen her
get so emotional before.

47
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:55,339
Thanks for looking out for us, Yui.

48
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:10,440
Um, Lady Asuna?

49
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:12,900
Who exactly are these new people?

50
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:15,140
Are they knights or mercenaries?

51
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:17,120
Oh, they're with me.

52
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,772
They're my best friends.

53
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:21,720
They came from the real world to help us.

54
00:04:28,980 --> 00:04:30,745
Thank you for your assistance.

55
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,360
I am so relieved.

56
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:33,874
To tell you the truth,

57
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:37,697
I thought everyone from your
world, aside from Lady Asuna,

58
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:40,309
of course, were brutes
like those soldiers.

59
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:43,037
Well, of course we're not all like that.

60
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:44,000
I'm Lisbeth.

61
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:44,990
Put her there, Mr.

62
00:04:45,073 --> 00:04:45,903
Knight.

63
00:04:45,986 --> 00:04:46,816
I'm Silica.

64
00:04:46,899 --> 00:04:47,729
It's nice to meet you.

65
00:04:47,812 --> 00:04:48,780
Oh, right. Apologies.

66
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:49,920
I am Renly.

67
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:51,707
A pleasure to meet you both.

68
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:54,670
Hey, Liz.

69
00:04:54,780 --> 00:04:57,015
How many people converted in with you?

70
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:58,780
Um, oh yeah.

71
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:01,157
Only a little over 2,000 came along.

72
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:05,320
I tried to get more, but even after
spilling my guts to the council,

73
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:06,953
that's all I could get.

74
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:09,480
It's more than enough.

75
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:12,617
But if reconverting is an
option for real worlders,

76
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:14,837
this could turn into a war of attrition.

77
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:18,017
We should focus on healing and
keep the front line from spreading.

78
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:19,460
We need a support unit.

79
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:23,097
Liz, Silica, could you fall
back with 200 and form one?

80
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:24,474
We'll get right on it.

81
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:26,227
Don't worry, we'll be ready.

82
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:28,477
I know how skilled you are in battle,

83
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:31,854
but if you're okay with it,
I need you to teach healing.

84
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:33,597
My world doesn't have sacred art.

85
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:36,397
So I thought if you and your
priests taught our warriors,

86
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:38,480
it might give us the edge we need.

87
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:39,600
Oh, yes.

88
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:40,760
I'd be happy to.

89
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:43,441
All right, then.

90
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:46,205
I'm heading to the front line.

91
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:05,000
Now that everyone's here, we won't lose.

92
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:29,300
We can beat them, I know it!

93
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:37,180
Together, we will win!

94
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:58,320
Man, I hope I logged them all in, in time.

95
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:01,830
You did.

96
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:04,860
I'm sure of it.

97
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:16,170
Damn it.

98
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:19,097
I should have anticipated
something like this.

99
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:23,897
When those girls told us the hijackers
logged American players into the underworld,

100
00:07:23,980 --> 00:07:25,440
I just went numb.

101
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:30,580
And on top of that, for some AI in
Asuna's phone to be the one that spots it,

102
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:33,000
I should turn in my keyboard.

103
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:35,737
Well, it happened the way it happened.

104
00:07:35,820 --> 00:07:38,277
Now that all these
civilians are logged in,

105
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:40,757
Project Alicization
isn't a secret anymore.

106
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:42,193
It's out in the public.

107
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:44,217
Yeah, that's a huge problem.

108
00:07:44,300 --> 00:07:46,297
But compared to the
enemy getting their hands

109
00:07:46,380 --> 00:07:48,797
on Alice and using her
to pilot war drones?

110
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:50,260
I prefer it.

111
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:54,000
She's special.

112
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:56,120
She's not an AI anymore.

113
00:07:56,680 --> 00:08:01,060
Alice is a new type of humanity, born
and raised in an alternate world.

114
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:02,500
She's the future.

115
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,580
And you knew that way before we did.

116
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:08,440
Isn't that right, Kirito?

117
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:15,010
Huh?

118
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:23,920
What the...

119
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:29,540
Hey, Harenko!

120
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:30,837
It's his Fluctlight!

121
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:32,508
Check out the activity log!

122
00:08:33,780 --> 00:08:35,297
What caused those spikes?

123
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:36,237
Don't know.

124
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:40,057
Whatever they were, they triggered
his consciousness at those two points.

125
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:42,460
But the log says he's still out of it.

126
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:45,278
Something made an impression though.

127
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:51,277
The timestamps check them.

128
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:55,301
I'll bet you anything those are
when the girls in the STLs dove in.

129
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:01,837
They are the same time.

130
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:06,977
Is it possible that all it took to make
him react were friends of his? Showing up.

131
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:08,097
Nah.

132
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:10,837
The kind of damage
Kirito's got can't be fixed

133
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:13,637
by some kind of poetic
explanation like that.

134
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,957
There's got to be a more logical reason.

135
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:17,437
The self.

136
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,397
The subject.

137
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:21,477
The image he has of
himself that defines him.

138
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:24,397
Could there be a backup
of that quantum pattern?

139
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:25,310
somewhere?

140
00:09:25,393 --> 00:09:27,020
No, of course there isn't.

141
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:29,880
We never made a copy
of Kirito's Fluctlight.

142
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:31,350
Hey.

143
00:09:31,433 --> 00:09:33,120
And even if there was a copy,

144
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:37,280
it'd be impossible to extract his
self-image and transfer it over.

145
00:09:37,780 --> 00:09:39,620
Higa, wait a sec. Maybe.

146
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:44,257
If there Was an active quantum pattern
that could Connect to his Fluctlight?

147
00:09:44,340 --> 00:09:46,046
but where would we find that?

148
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:47,600
Would you listen?

149
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:50,620
I'm listening.

150
00:09:50,940 --> 00:09:52,380
The subject observes.

151
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:54,080
The object is observed.

152
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:57,539
But you can't separate them
that clearly and easily.

153
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:59,010
Huh?

154
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:01,977
Subjective and objective
are just philosophical

155
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:04,617
concepts that explain the
relationship of things.

156
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:08,097
And since humans are social
creatures, not isolated individuals,

157
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:12,377
you have an image of others in your
mind, and they have one of you in theirs.

158
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:16,997
It's like we're all connected, up to a
point, in a kind of network, if you will.

159
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:18,198
Wouldn't you agree?

160
00:10:19,260 --> 00:10:22,257
The image of me in others?

161
00:10:22,340 --> 00:10:26,197
it's like a backup of the self-image

162
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:29,937
that's it we got it we can restore

163
00:10:30,020 --> 00:10:34,777
his subjective self-image we have the
data it's in the floodlights of the

164
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:41,717
people he's closest to all right we
want to extract that data we need an STL

165
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:47,540
and reproducing it'll take more than
one person we're gonna need two no three

166
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:49,070
people.

167
00:10:49,153 --> 00:10:53,000
Hey Keeks, the girls diving from
Roppongi, how tight are they with Kirito?

168
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:54,202
Are they close?

169
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:56,377
Yeah, they both are.

170
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:59,401
You heard about the Death
Gun case six months ago.

171
00:11:00,060 --> 00:11:01,677
Sinon helped Kirito crack that one.

172
00:11:01,760 --> 00:11:03,878
And Leafa is Kirito's little sister.

173
00:11:05,060 --> 00:11:06,000
This'll work!

174
00:11:06,180 --> 00:11:08,240
We got what we need to save Kirito!

175
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:10,320
We can restore his self-image!

176
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:12,577
We'll extract the image
of him stored in their

177
00:11:12,660 --> 00:11:15,257
Fluctlights and connect
it to the damaged regions!

178
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:20,617
That should Repair his subjective
self hot down this is gonna work.

179
00:11:20,700 --> 00:11:25,217
Oh no what am i saying this won't work?

180
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:30,340
The equipment i need to run everything
is in the main freaking control room.

181
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:34,577
Don't beat yourself up
Higa we have a better

182
00:11:34,660 --> 00:11:37,307
shot at restoring Kirito
now and that's good.

183
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:40,897
But for now we wait once
our guests leave and

184
00:11:40,980 --> 00:11:43,745
the ocean turtles ours
again we'll get to work.

185
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:45,680
That'll be too late.

186
00:11:45,940 --> 00:11:47,117
We have to do it now.

187
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:49,900
If the Asahi sends commandos to board us,

188
00:11:50,020 --> 00:11:52,757
and they end up fighting the
hijackers in the main shaft,

189
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:55,134
it could knock out the power in Subcon.

190
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,380
If that happens,

191
00:11:56,640 --> 00:12:00,317
Kirito's STL would shut down and
he'd be logged out of the Underworld.

192
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:01,230
Unconscious.

193
00:12:01,640 --> 00:12:02,470
us.

194
00:12:02,553 --> 00:12:06,762
In that state, we'd never get him to pass
the initialization stage, and he'll never

195
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:09,217
be able to connect to the STL again.

196
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:10,440
We can't wait.

197
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:12,200
We have to try.

198
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,260
Now, right now, while

199
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:18,297
he and those girls are
still in the underworld.

200
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:20,557
It's our only shot at saving him.

201
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:21,470
I'll do

202
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:23,277
it, Keeks. I'll go.

203
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:24,400
I don't follow.

204
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:25,976
Where are you going?

205
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:28,080
Alright, here's my plan.

206
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:32,157
There's a cable duct running down
the stern side of the main shaft.

207
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:35,480
It connects STL-2,
Kirito's room, to main con.

208
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:39,077
I'm going to climb down the duct until
I get to the maintenance connector.

209
00:12:39,160 --> 00:12:43,631
I'll patch into it, and I should be
able to control Kirito's STL from there.

210
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:48,497
But that connector is on the same
side of the bulkhead as the hijackers.

211
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:52,657
If they find out you're in the duct,
they'll breach it and attack you from below.

212
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:54,387
Right, so I'll need a decoy.

213
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:56,460
Yes, you do. But who?

214
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,420
Not who.

215
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:01,557
I wouldn't want anyone here
to risk their life too.

216
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:03,237
We'll unlock the bulkhead door,

217
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:07,117
then send some thing that can't get
killed on a walk downstairs to Minigun.

218
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,030
Him.

219
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:14,160
Oh, I get it. Ichemon.

220
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:15,760
Your robot?

221
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:17,549
But all it can do is walk.

222
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:19,994
It can't fight or run or anything else.

223
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:21,397
Once they see him coming,

224
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:24,517
they're just gonna blow it to
pieces and that's the end of that.

225
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:28,517
It sucks for Ichiemon, but
he's the best decoy we have.

226
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:33,129
Besides, with how he looks, they might
think he'll explode if they shoot him.

227
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:36,777
Well, he'll definitely get their
attention, that's for sure.

228
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:37,797
At the very least,

229
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:39,517
they might think we sent
him down there because

230
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:41,897
we're planning something
even more ridiculous.

231
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:43,274
They can't ignore him.

232
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:45,097
That's the point of sending him.

233
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:48,217
Then, while the hijackers
are dealing with Ichiemon,

234
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:50,377
I'll climb into the
lower part of the duct,

235
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:53,957
patch into that connector, and
operate Kirito's STL from there.

236
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:55,540
We have two robots.

237
00:13:56,220 --> 00:13:57,050
Hmm.

238
00:13:57,133 --> 00:13:59,160
We should send the aim on. Nope.

239
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:03,117
Like I told Asuna before this
nightmare started, he's not ready yet.

240
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:05,737
He needs a Fluctlight to
pilot and keep him in balance,

241
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:07,879
or he'll just roll down the stairs.

242
00:14:08,260 --> 00:14:09,090
Damn.

243
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:12,540
Higa, I'm not so sure about this.

244
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:14,260
Even if the decoy works,

245
00:14:14,460 --> 00:14:18,637
when you're in that duct you're vulnerable,
and if they find you in there...

246
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:21,737
You should take an agent to
keep an eye out while you work.

247
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:22,650
No way.

248
00:14:22,733 --> 00:14:26,000
The JSDF agents have to stay
here to keep all of you safe.

249
00:14:26,380 --> 00:14:29,792
Besides, the duct is way too
narrow for most folks to fit.

250
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:32,372
But not for a skinny little nerd like me.

251
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:34,101
Don't you worry.

252
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:36,692
I'll be down and back before you know it.

253
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:39,631
Hirito risked everything for this project.

254
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:43,897
If it weren't for him, Alice's Fluck Light
wouldn't have developed into what it is.

255
00:14:43,980 --> 00:14:45,600
He tried to protect her.

256
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:47,866
That's why he's in this mess.

257
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:53,177
And that's why if there's a chance
to save him I have to take it doesn't

258
00:14:53,260 --> 00:14:57,697
matter if I'm risking my life it's
the only way I can make it up to him

259
00:14:57,780 --> 00:15:03,997
um if you don't mind I'd like to go

260
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:07,417
with you and be your bodyguard I'm

261
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:11,497
pretty skinny myself but there's enough
meat on my bones to stop a bullet

262
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:15,737
But if it comes to that, I'm also the
one in charge of cable maintenance here,

263
00:15:15,820 --> 00:15:18,120
so it could be useful.

264
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:24,020
Uh, to be honest, I'm not 100 %
sure how far down that connector is.

265
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:27,107
If you're okay with it,
I could use the help.

266
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:28,380
Thanks, Yuna.

267
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:00,120
How boring.

268
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:04,760
Your soul is too thick
and heavy, too simple.

269
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:06,560
It sticks to my tongue.

270
00:16:07,980 --> 00:16:10,580
All you can think about is killing me.

271
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:13,320
And now you are done.

272
00:16:15,300 --> 00:16:16,880
That's what you'd think.

273
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:20,680
I still got some life in me.

274
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:24,260
Just a little longer.

275
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:29,180
Where is it?

276
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:30,400
Where'd it go?

277
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:33,120
Over there.

278
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:43,400
No, it wasn't that way.

279
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:46,800
Thirty seconds left.

280
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:52,460
There.

281
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:55,080
Found it.

282
00:16:56,800 --> 00:17:01,500
579, 580, 581, 582.

283
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:04,420
Now what could you possibly be up to?

284
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:14,940
I miss dammit forgive me Asuna and Alice.

285
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:16,760
He got me

286
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:27,820
Hey, I thought I told you to go back.

287
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:37,600
This is the first time you
disobeyed me, stubborn old dragon.

288
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:53,800
Oh Shagami, thanks for giving me
one more chance, I won't waste it.

289
00:18:15,020 --> 00:18:19,160
With the time-splitting
sword, I can cut two ways.

290
00:18:19,400 --> 00:18:22,400
The future and the past, you bastard.

291
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:29,240
Ahhhh!

292
00:18:53,320 --> 00:18:54,480
It's so warm.

293
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:01,300
Father…

294
00:19:07,180 --> 00:19:08,140
Uncle?

295
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,400
I remember.

296
00:19:12,700 --> 00:19:14,800
I was captured by Emperor Vecta.

297
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:20,680
Commander!

298
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:22,200
Uncle!

299
00:19:32,420 --> 00:19:33,520
Uncle, no.

300
00:19:47,840 --> 00:19:50,480
Come on, kiddo. Don't cry.

301
00:19:51,580 --> 00:19:56,020
We all gotta go sometime, and
this was just mine, that's all.

302
00:19:57,240 --> 00:20:01,380
You have to handle things on
your own now, but she'll be fine.

303
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:03,300
I know it.

304
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:07,460
You are my apprentice after
all, and my precious daughter.

305
00:20:09,460 --> 00:20:12,340
Oh well, at least we
went out in style, huh?

306
00:20:14,160 --> 00:20:14,990
Indeed.

307
00:20:15,073 --> 00:20:17,320
So many people will mourn your passing.

308
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:19,460
Consider yourself blessed.

309
00:20:21,540 --> 00:20:24,817
My lady, fancy seeing your ghost?

310
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:27,317
Here, I'm not a ghost, silly.

311
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:30,517
This is just the me that
exists in your memory,

312
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:37,477
the memory you had of Administrator
One, which you held dear in your soul.

313
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:38,580
Really,

314
00:20:39,340 --> 00:20:40,997
if you say so, my lady?

315
00:20:41,080 --> 00:20:41,917
Wow!

316
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:45,497
If that's how it is, then it's
good to know that you—I remember.

317
00:20:45,580 --> 00:20:47,874
remember I never could smile like that.

318
00:21:14,300 --> 00:21:16,557
I find it odd you don't despise me.

319
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:20,257
After all, I was the one who
forced immortality on you.

320
00:21:20,340 --> 00:21:22,700
And I kept robbing you of your memories.

321
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:25,937
I'll admit, after the first
hundred years it got old.

322
00:21:26,020 --> 00:21:29,120
But even so, my life
was pretty interesting.

323
00:21:30,300 --> 00:21:31,241
That's for sure.

324
00:21:31,900 --> 00:21:32,730
Good then.

325
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,940
I'm sorry, Fanatio.

326
00:21:41,220 --> 00:21:44,749
But it looks like we won't be
seeing each other for a while.

327
00:21:46,820 --> 00:21:48,380
Good luck down there.

328
00:21:56,540 --> 00:22:00,080
Make sure to give our baby
a happy life. You hear?

329
00:22:13,260 --> 00:22:14,220
They're going!

330
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:25,200
Do not worry, my commander.

331
00:22:25,760 --> 00:22:28,940
I swear, I will raise our child well.

332
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:33,360
They will be strong and brave
and proud like their father.

333
00:22:45,320 --> 00:22:46,820
Well, look who's up.

334
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:48,158
Good morning, boss.

335
00:22:48,340 --> 00:22:50,797
I guess you got your ass
kicked in there, huh?

336
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:51,939
What's the latest?

337
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:53,937
I did everything like you wanted.

338
00:22:54,020 --> 00:22:58,437
I sent in 50,000 players from the U
.S., and they're tearing it up in there.

339
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:01,460
Oh, and that jackass
Vassago got killed, too.

340
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:03,277
But he got excited about something.

341
00:23:03,360 --> 00:23:06,301
Had me convert his Gamer
account and dove back in.

342
00:23:07,080 --> 00:23:08,280
Really? Interesting.

343
00:23:08,840 --> 00:23:10,100
Not a bad idea.

344
00:23:16,260 --> 00:23:18,937
Critter, convert that
account to the Underworld.

345
00:23:19,020 --> 00:23:21,540
I still need to take care of some things.

346
00:23:35,820 --> 00:23:38,400
The next episode of SENDOW
